From 08d0c266d2598df3ba3f729dad9017035fe47cf5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:39:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): a local row keeps the stale-list open over its
 boot-snapshot copy [daveey]

The cold-start boot snapshot feeds this Mac's own replica rows into
mergeOfflineFallback (connection = registry primary), judged asleep at the
moment it was read. When a later local session list failed (backend event
loop stalled), a retained local row was replaced by that copy: offline_cached
without offline_stale_list, so the open was refused ("<hub> is offline") or
went read-only although the local gateway was running. With no connection_id
on the live row, identities did not match and the copy was added as a
refused duplicate instead.

- A retained row of the primary backend never yields to a replica copy; it
  takes the offline_stale_list stamp and resumes live with the notice.
- Merge identities treat an empty connection_id as the registry primary, so
  the boot copy is recognised as the same session (no duplicate).
- Remote rows with a replica copy keep today's behaviour.

Tests: integration (local row, with/without connection_id, opens live as one
row; remote asleep replica stays refused) and a merge unit test. Both new
local tests fail on the parent branch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
